--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Every decision function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN`.
--   JUST TRUE    the Rule says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the Rule says no in its own words: a "means" definition, a flat negative, an "if", "where" or "unless" unmet.
--   NOTHING      the Rule does not answer: a power limited by its own wording, a list that is not closed, a silence.

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 32 -- Administration and similar actions`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- definitions of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- “administration action” means an action for the administration under the direction of the Court of the estate of a
-- deceased person or for the execution under the direction of the Court of a trust.
-- src:4540 | 1. In this Order — “administration action” means an action for the administration under the direction of the Court of the estate of a deceased person or for the execution under the direction of the Court of a trust;
@ref O 32 r 1 “administration action” (src:4540)
GIVEN `the action is for the administration under the direction of the Court of the estate of a deceased person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the action is for the execution under the direction of the Court of a trust` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 32 r 1 an action is an administration action` MEANS
    IF `the action is for the administration under the direction of the Court of the estate of a deceased person` OR `the action is for the execution under the direction of the Court of a trust`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“administration action” means an action for the administration under the direction of the Court of the estate of a deceased person or for the execution under the direction of the Court of a trust"

-- “personal representatives” includes executors, administrators and trustees: a member is one, a non-member is not answered.
DECLARE `o 32 r 1 kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `o 32 r 1 an executor`
    `o 32 r 1 an administrator`
    `o 32 r 1 a trustee`
    `o 32 r 1 any other kind of person`

-- src:4541 | “personal representatives” includes executors, administrators and trustees.
@ref O 32 r 1 “personal representatives” (src:4541)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 32 r 1 kind of person`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 32 r 1 a person is a personal representative` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `o 32 r 1 any other kind of person` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“personal representatives” includes executors, administrators and trustees"
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

