§§ `Rule 3 -- parties`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:4560 | 3. —(1) All the personal representatives to which an administration or such an action as is referred to in Rule 2 relates must be parties to the action, and where the action is brought by personal representatives, any of them who does not consent to being joined as a claimant must be made a defendant. (2) All the persons having a beneficial interest in or claim against the estate or having a beneficial interest under the trust (as the case may be) to which such an action as is mentioned in paragraph (1) relates need not be parties to the action; but the claimant may make such of those persons, whether all or any one or more of them, parties as, having regard to the nature of the relief or remedy claimed in the action, the claimant thinks fit.
@ref O 32 r 3(1) all (src:4560)
GIVEN `the action is an administration action or an action referred to in Rule 2` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the personal representatives to which it relates are parties to the action` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 32 r 3(1) all the personal representatives are parties to the action` MEANS
    IF `the action is an administration action or an action referred to in Rule 2`
    THEN IF `all the personal representatives to which it relates are parties to the action`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (a requirement not met; O 3 r 2(1) makes every requirement subject to the Court's discretion, so the text does not itself say no): "All the personal representatives to which an administration or such an action as is referred to in Rule 2 relates must be parties to the action" (a bare must not done; open convention question QB)
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the trigger is unmet, so the duty does not arise; `o 32 r 3(1) all the personal representatives are parties to the action (the duty arises)` says so (open convention question QD)
@ref O 32 r 3(1) all (src:4560)
GIVEN `the action is an administration action or an action referred to in Rule 2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 32 r 3(1) all the personal representatives are parties to the action (the duty arises)` MEANS
    IF `the action is an administration action or an action referred to in Rule 2`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "All the personal representatives to which an administration or such an action as is referred to in Rule 2 relates must be parties to the action"
