      `the claim is in respect of a debt or other liability and is made against the estate by a person not a party to the action` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court directs or allows the party to appear in addition to, or in substitution for, the executors or administrators` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 32 r 3(3) the Court may direct or allow another party to appear` MEANS
    IF `the claim is made in proceedings under a judgment or order given in an action for the administration of the estate of a deceased person` AND `the claim is in respect of a debt or other liability and is made against the estate by a person not a party to the action`
    THEN IF `the Court directs or allows the party to appear in addition to, or in substitution for, the executors or administrators`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the Court may direct or allow any other party to appear either in addition to, or in substitution for, the executors or administrators on such terms as to costs or otherwise as the Court thinks fit"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the Court may direct or allow any other party to appear either in addition to, or in substitution for, the executors or administrators on such terms as to costs or otherwise as the Court thinks fit"

