    IF `an administration action is brought by a creditor of the estate of a deceased person or by a person claiming to be entitled under a will or on the intestacy or to be beneficially entitled under a trust` AND `the claimant alleges that no or insufficient accounts have been provided by the personal representatives`
    THEN IF `the Court stays the proceedings for a period specified in the order and orders that the personal representatives provide the claimant with proper accounts within that period`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where an administration action is brought by a creditor of the estate of a deceased person or by a person claiming to be entitled under a will or on the intestacy of a deceased person or to be beneficially entitled under a trust, and the claimant alleges that no or insufficient accounts have been provided by the personal representatives (as the case may be) then, without affecting its other powers, the Court may — order that proceedings in the action be stayed for a period specified in the order and that the personal representatives must within that period provide the claimant with proper accounts"
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an administration action is brought by a creditor of the estate of a deceased person or by a person claiming to be entitled under a will or on the intestacy of a deceased person or to be beneficially entitled under a trust, and the claimant alleges that no or insufficient accounts have been provided by the personal representatives (as the case may be) then, without affecting its other powers, the Court may — order that proceedings in the action be stayed for a period specified in the order and that the personal representatives must within that period provide the claimant with proper accounts"
