GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 32 r 5(2)(b) the Court may give judgment or make an order for administration` MEANS
    IF `an administration action is brought by a creditor of the estate of a deceased person or by a person claiming to be entitled under a will or on the intestacy or to be beneficially entitled under a trust` AND `the claimant alleges that no or insufficient accounts have been provided by the personal representatives` AND `it is necessary to prevent proceedings by other creditors or by other persons claiming to be entitled in the same manner`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if necessary to prevent proceedings by other creditors or by other persons claiming to be entitled in the same manner, give judgment or make an order for the administration of the estate to which the action relates, and include in the judgment or order for administration an order that no proceedings are to be taken under the judgment or order, or under any particular account or inquiry directed, without the permission of the Judge in person"

-- r 6: the personal representatives have the conduct of the sale "unless the Court otherwise directs".
-- src:4570 | 6. Where in an administration action an order is made for the sale of any property vested in personal representatives, those personal representatives have the conduct of the sale unless the Court otherwise directs.
@ref O 32 r 6 (src:4570)
GIVEN `in an administration action an order is made for the sale of property vested in personal representatives` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court otherwise directs` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 32 r 6 the personal representatives have the conduct of the sale` MEANS
    IF `in an administration action an order is made for the sale of property vested in personal representatives`
    THEN IF `the Court otherwise directs`
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Court otherwise directs"
         ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where in an administration action an order is made for the sale of any property vested in personal representatives"
